{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1494321062,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyMjcyOTkwMTI=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1505","origin":"github"},"title":"`get_paths_by_dataset()` is MAJOR source of slowdown!","message":"@bpoldrack @yarikoptic This is the climax of the OPT saga of the past few days:\n\nLet me introduce you to: `get_paths_by_dataset()`, a function that runs every time a path is passed into almost any top-level command. Now watch this (with our big collection):\n\n````\n% time DATALAD_LOG_LEVEL=debug \\\n  python -c \"import datalad.api; from datalad.interface.utils import get_paths_by_dataset; get_paths_by_dataset(['$PWD'], recursive=True)\"\n\u003csnip\u003e\nDATALAD_LOG_LEVEL=debug python -c   1,31s user 1,10s system 18% cpu 12,744 total\n\n# and now for fun and games, we give the same path twice\nmih@meiner /tmp/datasets.datalad.org (git)-[master] % time DATALAD_LOG_LEVEL=debug \\\n  python -c \"import datalad.api; from datalad.interface.utils import get_paths_by_dataset; get_paths_by_dataset(['$PWD', '$PWD'], recursive=True)\"\n\u003csnip\u003e\nDATALAD_LOG_LEVEL=debug python -c   2,14s user 2,09s system 16% cpu 25,093 total\n````\n\nSo this is not only slow, it is also stupid. I can say that, I wrote it.\n\nI see no way how to make the individual pieces faster. If we ask for the full list of datasets in a tree, we have to get them at some point (which does not mean we should carefully evaluate when to ask for such a list). However, the logic purely within that function could be improved. In particular wrt the wasteful rediscovery when multiple input paths are given (even beyond a plain `unique(paths)`).\n\nI won't have time to work on this now, but if you ever feel something is slow, consider throwing some computer science in this approximate direction first!","files":null}]}